{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.132284Z","id":"d0a80285b0b3fcb2450558fea43c995c6bf9e0627b0580709fd093db3c92a1b8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:caee7184224e","summary":"Fixed in git:caee71842 (with 7abc1ef16). Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Follow-up to the 7abc1ef16 fix: the cache-write tail now applies on the Messages API alone (record 6f80a64b). pricing::the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_cache_write_rate and pricing::off_the_messages_api_the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_input_rate pass. Commit caee71842; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","supersedes":"827df625c91cfc9e6bd45747f9298c80317d4ca3ae53a9d40fdd6fdce6f1aa1c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.225260Z","id":"02cd038648139c93618dd8830bb63c3a2133ad4547fb06e63db6346adaff950f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:caee7184224e","summary":"Fixed in git:caee71842. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed: affordable()'s doc comment is reflowed and states the per-API input pricing. Commit caee71842; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","supersedes":"1b312b12dab558d0ee46c32ade8694f39ffe1cb3c6d882223197905cc5da7995","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.317617Z","id":"8d00faf5d82ddc13bfd4c030f277e204e0a160f64b0b4a91aa3fc8b41933857f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:caee7184224e","summary":"Fixed in git:caee71842. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed: affordable() prices the uncached input at cache_write only when settings.api is ModelApi::Anthropic, at the input rate on openai and gemini. Test pricing::off_the_messages_api_the_input_bound_is_priced_at_the_input_rate (both APIs: a dear cache-write rate does not bound the turn, a dear input rate stops it credits_exhausted) passes. Commit caee71842; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (integration 'test result: ok. 60 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored', lib '25 passed'). Proposed close.","supersedes":"6f80a64bd422620dbb688667209235a5f684d167abf6c61c497f3ba1c333ede8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.412918Z","id":"01b073b21daf1c35c733bc184227951a0884a6b9a7854e06b4af657afce95904","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7abc1ef162f1","summary":"Fixed in git:7abc1ef16. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed in git:7abc1ef16: the turn keeps the rates its answering attempt snapshotted (call_rates) and charges the committed rows at them. money::a_repeated_call_is_priced_as_it_was_made and pricing::a_billed_cost_survives_a_resumed_run pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","supersedes":"16e5088f83fd02c99e03041e121b8aa3d37cb7e039648ce126c5ba45563d44dd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T00:37:08.508048Z","id":"58dc052aa688b685650f230514d7e646d6bbbc553c96f1c78f26a1746c712248","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7abc1ef162f1","summary":"Fixed in git:7abc1ef16. Evidence, from the reply on this thread: Fixed in git:7abc1ef16: run::tests::a_mixed_card_bills_the_cost_based_rows_and_keeps_the_credit_based_ones, a_row_over_a_million_tokens_falls_short_by_under_its_millions, a_billed_cost_of_0_charges_no_credits_on_cost_based_rows and a_billed_row_without_a_snapshotted_rate_is_resolved_before_billing pass; bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passed (lib and integration: 'test result: ok. 59 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored'); SHAs are unsigned and change on re-signing. Proposed close.","supersedes":"87e8296d8c6e5e6657e3d05933954369313255f0d264b7a12a84741629fb9c3b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:19:13.364654Z","id":"fea59b4e1e486287218d23962cc8d6b7ad830e0ddb1d8f7080b53bea600268dd","body":{"detail":"The Performer::Web arm answers web_disabled (uncharged, journaled like a policy refusal) whatever the run's WebShape (crates/clax-bot/src/web/access.rs) declares, so a run whose prompt declares clax.web.search or clax.web.fetch (crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs dts) is told it may call them and is refused at each call. Nothing declares them yet in production: Bot::web_configured is false on both hosts (crates/clax-http/src/bot.rs, crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs), so start_run (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs) writes web \"\" on every run. The arm is to be replaced by the checks of spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md §4.2 and §6.3 (declared, enabled now, cap, URL rule and sources, page store, credits, source call, Spend transaction) before any host sets web_configured.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"4997f45140a6505b678c91a181384005fa67eccc345ba222f7b948efd626430b"},"summary":"Every clax.web.* call is refused web_disabled: RunHost::perform has no web source to call yet","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:19:13.364744Z","id":"95102b6355d5b44fab68c0004ac7b4e695a99626bbbfcb5314918fe4fd1781f9","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md §6.1 declares `format?: \"auto\" | \"raw\"`. api::Ty has no string-literal type, so the declaration (crates/clax-bot/src/api.web.d.ts.golden) says `format?: string` and the op's doc names the two values; check_args accepts any string, so the performer must refuse any other value invalid_args. A Ty::Lit (TypeScript literal, JSON Schema const, checked by check_args) would put the two values in the declaration and the argument check.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":556},"end":{"line":563},"content_hash":"3a84c23cc3d1c0ab39858c3dcd8496912f01d989aa63b3da1d135d867591607a"},"summary":"web.fetch's opts.format is declared `string`, not the spec's `\"auto\" | \"raw\"`","tags":["revisit:a script passes a format other than auto or raw, or a second operation takes an enumerated string","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:27:39.405901Z","id":"0112a7caeddde42e39c2aa4d3ddba9e45ae91012f9164d9cf3335474e42440f4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:680a2c05c","summary":"Taken: api::Ty::Enum declares web.fetch's opts.format as \"auto\" | \"raw\" (crates/clax-bot/src/api.web.d.ts.golden), its JSON Schema as a string enum, and check_args refuses another value invalid_args. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test passes api::tests::the_sandbox_knows_every_op_whatever_the_shape (format \"html\" -> 'argument 2 (opts).format must be one of auto, raw') and dts_with_web_matches_its_golden.","supersedes":"95102b6355d5b44fab68c0004ac7b4e695a99626bbbfcb5314918fe4fd1781f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:45:47.404481Z","id":"b4d21d32af9823099ac6db0c7c88cc061b7c249f3689d0f07ff5eb45f829e80f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fea59b4e1e486287218d23962cc8d6b7ad830e0ddb1d8f7080b53bea600268dd","summary":"Replaced in git:53a0db82a: the Performer::Web arm of RunHost::perform now calls RunHost::web (crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs), which performs web.search and web.fetch through Deps::web with the shape, grant, URL rule, page store, cap, credit and Spend checks; a run whose Deps::web is None still answers web_disabled. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration passes, including web::a_search_then_a_fetch_of_a_result_is_answered_and_charged_twice and web::a_host_without_a_source_refuses_web_disabled. Proposed close: fixed in git:53a0db82a.","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:30:16.869644Z","id":"1eca5f36b16770e4c15ee7fa62b01f9414778800bfcd1d8c77a756e186431374","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:53a0db82a","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"065cc6f618c77ab4276af696b2d7a7e5db54b6f35cd6acc112b3643e7c465933"},"summary":"Fixed in git:53a0db82a: the Performer::Web arm of RunHost::perform calls RunHost::web (crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:integration passes in just check on this branch, including web::a_search_then_a_fetch_of_a_result_is_answered_and_charged_twice; a run whose Deps::web is None still answers web_disabled (web::a_host_without_a_source_refuses_web_disabled).","supersedes":"fea59b4e1e486287218d23962cc8d6b7ad830e0ddb1d8f7080b53bea600268dd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:03.791144Z","id":"ca3998787245b12150aa8aeda83f2044691a20c0ba99cbf17aec33c0cff97ff8","body":{"detail":"Live step_done events carry the step's charge from Store::commit_step; the canonical events rebuilt from committed steps read payload.credits_milli, which the payload never has (the charge is computed at commit), so a client that reconnects sees credits only in run_credits_milli. The store could return the step's charge with the steps (a sum of its usage rows) for the replay.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":375},"end":{"line":386},"content_hash":"34ff05f6f3e85c32427c32135770237712eccad0757f384b6ab5900b617140d8"},"summary":"A replayed step_done carries no credits for its step","supersedes":"b31ddcab70856e03c45a23685389874c5e7d4a5e4103a27abd7d20451e7e8c48","tags":["events","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:13.241401Z","id":"cc909e26f6eacfdea24fb1788dd783f4d07128c132005edea9be1b9d37815c57","body":{"detail":"A run's history keeps the blocks its provider produced: Gemini turns hold a `signature` field on text and tool_use blocks (crates/clax-sample/src/messages/gemini.rs), and Chat Completions turns hold thinking blocks with an empty signature (openai.rs). RunSettings is read before every tick, so after an admin switches api to anthropic an open run sends these to the Messages API, which refuses the unknown field and the unsigned thinking; the run ends model_error. Switching between openai and gemini drops or mistranslates nothing fatal.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (fa547d92), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"02de2c3a46cb7f229c289416253894e26660ad5d5d58decf7b59d8237bf0879c"},"suggested_fix":"Record the API a run started on (its row, like its model) and keep it for the run, or strip foreign fields when the Messages API is the target.","summary":"Changing the API while runs are open sends one API's blocks to another","supersedes":"6633378c7efec4a4886033f0ea1d6de83b89ba295da428262a746662c841ddd0","tags":["providers","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:13.375296Z","id":"c675ccb277d8d17449b1880c6972fb3fe9b6ee64099e5219d98c4afdaa335767","body":{"detail":"Spec section 8: locally a value in config.toml or the environment overrides the stored one. from_store reads Store::bot_setting and leaves per_person_concurrency, lease and renewal at their defaults; the daemon's SettingsSource must apply HomeConfig::bot (including bot.per_person_concurrency and enabled) on top, re-read per tick.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (2f8fe438), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved. Reply 67173b9e on the original proposed a close: the server lays [bot] over the database inside the store (Store::set_bot_overrides), fixed in git:bf3458ec.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"ea413dee711a57207ddc291eb3872d8297bd0a023361d0b7c7a7930cf7dd7878"},"summary":"RunSettings::from_store reads the database only: the [bot] config overrides are the server's to lay over it","supersedes":"6b0f4fa3625e588a7b1a9b5d168c2475eface331b571b6b2c84bd0d6ac95ea3f","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:13.515654Z","id":"06b231efca2d53f3527a7cbfac8863544ea10b5abd030c5991e4245bbe49d3d3","body":{"detail":"tick reads run_with_steps and History::of parses each payload (assistant blocks, script code and outcome, the first turn's system prompt) to rebuild the messages, so a run of N steps does O(N) work and reads O(total payload) per tick, O(N^2) over the run. Bounded by max_steps (40 by default); a cache of the history keyed by the last committed step would make it O(1).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (94a4332d), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":590},"end":{"line":651},"content_hash":"8e8e29c05e8e590bdae85e7966b0796756cd3f0ef6d45a96e7331f6b3d060f26"},"summary":"Every tick rebuilds the whole history from every committed step's payload","supersedes":"d5508d796427ba5e37c93c32f1e686b7f316a843b1af9c392e80837b013a5b78","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:13.655722Z","id":"2dd0bd4e1072dfeedd198cfb6af0d2358bb7a835cad07b52e539ddc5ab3cdaba","body":{"detail":"usage_rows stores cost as ceil(qty x rate / base) of an integer rate (charge_in, crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs). For qty <= base the share is hit exactly; above it the rows' costs may sum to slightly less than the billed cost. Exact sums would need the store to take a billed cost per row rather than a rate.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (47f96906), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":865},"end":{"line":935},"content_hash":"c540eaa6b294efa7579537cb080ac1566d4ec86f91dd306da0d9f3122c457fc4"},"summary":"bill() sets an integer micro-USD-per-million rate, so a row of more than a million tokens can fall short of its billed share by under qty / 1 000 000 micro-USD","supersedes":"88cb08afd2df76a43228e215ac8303f6f063bbecbcf4b4eddfd5db739880ab04","tags":["pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:13.788352Z","id":"39f9607f8178bccd60f64d8e9169741f2d8a4faab086848379242375b77ddb82","body":{"detail":"Without a rate the commit fails unknown_cost_line (charge_in). Dropping the rows would hide the tokens from the person's usage; a new RateSource needs a store migration (usage_rows.rate_source CHECK). The row charges 0 either way, being waived for an own key.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (123e4f52), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":937},"end":{"line":960},"content_hash":"68d3664e4bfe1d629fe1a91f1b256044aaf9f5db75d72f780f9435cdbc170c94"},"summary":"token_rate gives an own-key turn on a model with no rate a waived zero rate sourced 'default', rather than dropping its token rows or adding a RateSource for it","supersedes":"24b77e73e19e5b7c4703e8c71abb49197f4d9c26c4b087fec1d289a1b6460c02","tags":["pricing","revisit:the store gains a rate source for waived or unpriced rows","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:13.922745Z","id":"aef2e8a1241479d0cf2616a297ba1847599f0301ad056c7cd49dfd042c90ca1e","body":{"detail":"With infra_lines on (the Worker), each step charges do.requests = 1 + its host calls and toolpath.storage = the payload's JSON bytes for 30 days. Neither is read from Cloudflare's billing: spec section 13 lists this as a known gap. The payload holds the script's code and outcome, so storage scales with output, not with what the journal keeps.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (6f3e5c2c), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1066},"end":{"line":1085},"content_hash":"209d50573adc6aa561185d99669f36da87ff8d0d43beac8cdb8692b1060c2e1e"},"summary":"Durable Object requests and Toolpath storage are estimated per step","supersedes":"9ef3eb11192d0472f341bc0950aac098e7fa04f25ef75f49a69f2f6b9fe65d74","tags":["credits","gap","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:14.053779Z","id":"3d514de71cd928bb44457f55b6e05ae51d68a64c17d210bb52babdf8314d84e5","body":{"detail":"Tick::affordable prices the request as its JSON bytes / 4 tokens, the part the last turn cached at the cached-input rate and the rest at the input rate, then caps max_tokens to the output the credits left pay for. A request whose tokens run well above bytes/4 (non-Latin text, dense JSON) can still overshoot the person's credits by its input; counting tokens (the Messages API count_tokens endpoint) would bound it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from its original record by mailto:alex@kesling.co (96939966), after crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs moved. Since a9ecb07d1 the uncached rest is priced at the cache-write rate, not the input rate.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1742},"end":{"line":1835},"content_hash":"3216d8f8631b18b19db0edf730c55858479f00e599dfeeee83f821fa275f76ad"},"summary":"A turn's affordable max_tokens rests on a byte-count estimate of its input","supersedes":"512cb24a0272168d831772fd11480f5c977e3120110dd14ad03ff4a19ff89b26","tags":["credits","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
